From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 22:53:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Lophinya: exp - restore interrupt flag in
 RegionParallelRunner's barrier wait

InterruptedException was being swallowed alongside TimeoutException/
ExecutionException. Split it into its own catch that calls
Thread.currentThread().interrupt() before falling through to the same
drop-this-entity handling, per the standard JDK convention of letting the
flag survive an InterruptedException catch instead of eating it.

exp/* isolated exploration branch. Not for merge into ver/26.2-nya.

diff --git a/src/main/java/fun/bm/lophinya/parallel/RegionParallelRunner.java b/src/main/java/fun/bm/lophinya/parallel/RegionParallelRunner.java
index a7776d4cafaa50673273e6eb9e3b16aff8fbf46d..f0a7af5a19bab3196e173f43cb681bc8f774777a 100644
--- a/src/main/java/fun/bm/lophinya/parallel/RegionParallelRunner.java
+++ b/src/main/java/fun/bm/lophinya/parallel/RegionParallelRunner.java
@@ -126,13 +126,21 @@ public final class RegionParallelRunner {
                 }
                 result = future.get(remaining, TimeUnit.NANOSECONDS);
                 stats.computedInTime++;
-            } catch (final TimeoutException | InterruptedException | ExecutionException giveUp) {
+            } catch (final TimeoutException | ExecutionException giveUp) {
                 // Deadline missed (or the worker itself failed): drop this entity for this tick and
                 // move on. compute() must tolerate being abandoned mid-run - it never touches shared
                 // state, so an orphaned computation is wasted CPU, not a correctness problem.
                 future.cancel(true);
                 stats.timedOut++;
                 continue;
+            } catch (final InterruptedException interrupted) {
+                // Restore the interrupt flag rather than swallowing it - this thread (the region
+                // owner thread) did not ask to stop, but whoever interrupted it might expect the
+                // usual JDK convention of the flag surviving past this catch.
+                Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
+                future.cancel(true);
+                stats.timedOut++;
+                continue;
             }
 
             // Re-validate immediately before commit - never trust snapshot-time state. This single
